/bin/
/dist/
# `go build ./cmd/autodb/` writes the binary into the working directory, so a
# `git add -A` sweeps 30-odd MB into the tree. It happened once; the name is
# the package's, so it will happen again.
/autodb
*.test
coverage.out
.env

# Local Go workspace — points at sibling checkouts on THIS machine, so
# it must never be committed (it would break every other clone and CI).
go.work
go.work.sum

# auto-agents workspace mailbox (v0.2.30+)
.auto-agents/

# Neovim's own log, written into the cwd when a headless test run cannot
# create its server socket. A test artifact, never source. auto-core already
# ignores this; autodb did not, so a suite run left the tree dirty.
nvim.log

# autodb-test.sh per-run logs and ledgers (see shared/playbooks/autodb-test-harness.md)
.autodb-test-logs/
